s</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Reinert</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Seiler</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilman</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Scharf</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bullock</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Normobaric hyperoxia-induced improvement in cerebral metabolism and reduction in intracranial pressure in patients with severe brain injury</article-title><source>J Neurosurg</source><year>2004</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>435</fpage><lpage>444</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15352601</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bottini</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Jagiella</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Westphal</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ford</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rockswold</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Loewenson</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A pilot study of hyperbaric oxygen in the treatment of human stroke</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>1991</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>1137</fpage><lpage>1142</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1926256</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nighoghossian</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Trouillas</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Adeleine</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Salord</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hyperbaric oxygen in the treatment of acute ischemic stroke. A double blind pilot study</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>1995</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>1369</fpage><lpage>1372</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7631339</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rusyniac</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirk</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>May</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kao</surname><given-names>LW</given-names></name><name><surname>Brizendine</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Welch</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cordell</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Alonso</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hyperbaric oxygen therapy in acute ischemic stroke: results of the hyperbaric oxygen in acute ischemic stroke trial pilot study</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>2003</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>571</fpage><lpage>574</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12574578</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singhal</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oxygen therapy in stroke: past, present and future</article-title><source>Int J Stroke</source><year>2006</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>191</fpage><lpage>200</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18706016</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saugstad</surname><given-names>OD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Resuscitation with room air or oxygen supplementation</article-title><source>Clin Perinatol</source><year>1998</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>741</fpage><lpage>756</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9779345</pub-id></citation></